See
.I variables
and
.I expansion
(2.2, 3.4).
.IP variables
Variables in
.I csh
hold one or more strings as value.
The most common use of variables is in controlling the behavior
of the shell.
See
.I path,
.I noclobber,
and
.I ignoreeof
for examples.
Variables such as
.I argv
are also usto be done last or we may lose
