.I \&.login
also in your home directory.
This file contains commands which you wish to do each time you login
to the \s-2UNIX\s0 system.
My
.I \&.login
file looks something like:
.DS
tset \-d adm3a \-p adm3a
fixexrc
set history=20
set time=3
