exitstat()
{

	/*
	 * Note that if STATUS is corrupted (i.e. getn bombs)
	 * then error will exit directly because we poke child here.
	 * Otherwise we might continue unwarrantedly (sic).
	 */
	child++;
	exit(getn(value("status")));
}

/*
 * Catch an interrupt, e.g. during leno argument is given then change to the home directory of the user.
.PP
If
.I name
is not found as a subdirectory of the current directory
(and does not begin with `/', `./', or `../'),
then each component of the variable
.I cdpath
is checked to see if it has a subdirectory
.IR name .
Finally, if all else fails but
.I name
is a shell variable whose value begins with `/',
